-- ===========================================================================
-- Warlock / Demonology: talent DBC rewrites and renames
-- ===========================================================================
--
-- Third file of the Demonology batch.  Rewrites the talent rank spells
-- themselves: new effect layouts, renames and tooltips.  Depends on the custom
-- spells defined in woa_2026_08_02_02.sql and is completed by the
-- `spell_pet_auras` / `spell_proc` / `spell_script_names` rows in files 04-06.
--
-- Renames in this file:
--     Improved Imp            -> Imperious Flames
--     Improved Health Funnel  -> Sacrifice of Blood
--     Improved Succubus       -> Demonic Lash
--     Master Conjuror         -> Fel Attunement
--
--
-- THE CLASS-MASK COLUMN TRAP
--
--   The nine EffectSpellClassMask columns are stored in the DBC as
--   [effect][word] -- columns 122-130 are
--       effect1.A effect1.B effect1.C  effect2.A effect2.B effect2.C  effect3.*
--   but spell_dbc.py names them A1 A2 A3 B1 B2 B3 C1 C2 C3.  So the triple
--   "A1 A2 A3" is EFFECT 1's three words, NOT word A of effects 1/2/3.
--
--   Verified three ways: 18703 Improved Health Funnel masks Health Funnel's
--   word-A flag (16777216) on both of its spellmods, and stores it in A1 and
--   B1; 30319 Demonic Resilience's effect-2 mask sits in B2; and no warlock
--   spell anywhere has SpellFamilyFlags1 & 4, which is what "B1 = 4" on 47245
--   Molten Core would have to mean under the naive reading.
--
--   Every effect slot this file repurposes therefore has ALL THREE of its own
--   words zeroed.  Several talents ship stale garbage in words the base game
--   never read (47230 Fel Synergy effect-2 word B = 16384, 18705 Demonic
--   Brutality effect-2 word C = 8, 30143 Demonic Aegis effect-1 word B =
--   536870944); leaving those behind would silently mask the new dummies
--   against unrelated spells.
--
--
-- WHY SO MANY EFFECTS BECOME SPELL_AURA_DUMMY
--
--   Two reasons, often at once.  A dummy is how a talent hands a number to its
--   AuraScript (read back with GetAuraEffect(...)->GetAmount()), and it is the
--   only effect shape `spell_pet_auras` will anchor to -- SpellMgr.cpp:2470
--   rejects any row whose effect is neither SPELL_EFFECT_DUMMY nor
--   APPLY_AURA/SPELL_AURA_DUMMY.
--
--   Tooltip numbers use DieSides 1, so every displayed N is stored as N-1
--   (SpellEffectInfo::CalcValue, SpellInfo.cpp:431).  Anchors that carry no
--   number use DieSides 0.
--
--
-- DEMONIC BRUTALITY NEEDS A PRIVATE FAMILY BIT
--
--   Torment (3716), Suffering (17735) and Consume Shadows (17767) all carry
--   SpellFamilyFlags = 33554432 (word A bit 25), so a SPELLMOD_COOLDOWN class
--   mask cannot reduce Suffering's cooldown without also reducing the other
--   two.  The Suffering rank chain is re-flagged onto word C bit 16
--   (SpellFamilyFlags2 = 65536).  Word C is NOT unused by the warlock family --
--   scanning all 49919 spells, the union of SpellFamilyFlags2 across family 5
--   is 0x0000FDFF (bit 0 Inferno Effect, bit 7 Fel Domination, bit 12 Demonic
--   Empowerment, bit 13 Metamorphosis, bit 14 Soul Link, bit 15 Dark Pact, and
--   so on).  Nothing however uses bit 16 or anything above it, so 16 is free
--   and 17 goes to 200420 Molten Fury.  Word-A bit 25 is left intact so nothing
--   that keys off it changes.  Rank chain taken from `spell_ranks`.
--
--   Suffering's cooldown lives in CategoryRecoveryTime (120000) under Category
--   84, with RecoveryTime 0.  Creature::AddSpellCooldown applies the owner's
--   SPELLMOD_COOLDOWN to BOTH values, and because the spell has a category it
--   takes the `if (categorycooldown && ...)` branch, so 120000 - 90000 = 30000
--   is what actually lands.  Two notes on that path:
--
--     * The same modifier is also applied to `spellcooldown`, which is 0 here.
--       It is a uint32, so a flat -90000 wraps it -- but that value is only
--       read in the `else if (spellcooldown)` branch, which the category branch
--       has already skipped.  Harmless for Suffering specifically; worth
--       knowing before pointing a flat cooldown mod at a pet spell whose
--       cooldown is NOT category-based.
--
--     * The category branch stamps the cooldown onto every spell sharing the
--       category.  Torment is Category 36 and Suffering is Category 84, so
--       they do not bleed into each other.
--
--   Note the class mask must sit on effect 1's word C (column
--   EffectSpellClassMaskA3 -- see the naming trap above), matching the
--   SpellFamilyFlags2 bit set on the Suffering ranks below.
--
--
-- MOLTEN CORE KEEPS ITS ORIGINAL PROC
--
--   Effect1 (PROC_TRIGGER_SPELL -> 47383 at ranks 1-2, 71165 at rank 3) and
--   Effect2 (Immolate duration) are untouched, per-rank ProcFlags included
--   (ranks 1-2 are 327680, rank 3 is 262144 -- inconsistent in the base data,
--   left exactly as shipped).
--
--   ProcChance does move, 4/8/12 -> 100, because ProcChance is a spell-wide
--   field and the new Effect3 has to fire on every Shadow Bolt.  The original
--   per-rank chance is not lost -- the AuraScript rolls it itself in a
--   CheckEffectProc bound to EFFECT_0, so Corruption's proc rate is unchanged.
--
--   NO `spell_proc` ROW IS ADDED FOR 47245/47246/47247.  A spell_proc row
--   replaces the whole spell's DBC proc configuration, which would silently
--   break the Corruption proc.  Effect-level separation is done with class
--   masks (Effect3 is masked to Shadow Bolt alone) plus per-effect
--   CheckEffectProc, which AuraEffect::CheckEffectProc evaluates independently
--   for each effect.
--




